---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /writing/
title: Writing
description: Dated essays, announcements, and explorations from the Design Lasagna kitchen.
---
<div class="writing-page">
  <header class="writing-page__header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Writing</p>
    <h1>Notes from<br><em>the kitchen.</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">Dated essays, announcements, and explorations — the thinking behind Design Lasagna's tools, kept out of the reference docs.</p>
    <p><a href="/writing/feed.xml" rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml">RSS feed</a></p>
  </header>

  {% set articles = collections.writing | writingNewestFirst %}
  {% if articles.length %}
  <div class="writing-list">
    {% for article in articles %}
    <article class="writing-entry">
      <p class="writing-entry__meta">{{ article.date | dateISO }}{% for tag in article.data.tags | writingTags %} · {{ tag }}{% endfor %}</p>
      <div>
        <h2><a href="{{ article.url }}">{{ article.data.title }}</a></h2>
        <p>{{ article.data.description }}</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% else %}
  <p>Nothing has been written here yet.</p>
  {% endif %}

  <footer class="writing-note">
    <p>Writing is chronological: posts are dated when they are published and are not rewritten afterward. For exact contracts and setup, read the <a href="/docs/">docs</a>; for what each tool does and where to start, see <a href="/tools/">Tools</a>; for what we are building and why, start with <a href="/about/">About Design Lasagna</a>.</p>
  </footer>
</div>
